From 5b35a0afaffd93a6bf6b47cbbd8ec79147b0d774 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:22:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): widen long-context indexer top-k segments and
 reuse source blocks

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488.

Rationale:
Long-context V4.1 indexer top-k selection (IndexerTopK at widths 64K..1M) previously stored order-preserving 16-bit BF16 keys (_key16) in 4-byte T.int32 shared-memory arrays, capping each segment CTA at _SEGMENT_ENTRIES = 4096 entries and each merge CTA at _MERGE_KEYS = 8192 keys. Furthermore:
1. Per-thread contiguous reads (keys[tx * per + v]) during ordered compaction suffered 8-way to 32-way shared-memory bank conflicts across warps, and every thread re-read keys[tx * per + v] in the second compaction pass even when its slice had zero winners.
2. Stage-1 and merge CTAs initialized and scanned the full compile-time segment/merge capacity even when the row active extent was smaller.
3. On candidate-publishing source layers (Layer 20, candidate_blocks=True, width > 16384), IndexerV41Plan ran both select_blocks (top-2048 blocks of 8 = 16,384 positions over the full 1M row) and a full-width select (top-512 individual positions over the full 1M row), even though every top-512 position is guaranteed to reside inside the top-2048 blocks.

Optimize long-context IndexerTopK and IndexerV41Plan while preserving exact score-then-lowest-position tie-breaking and ascending output order:
1. Store shared-memory keys and sel_key as T.uint16 for topk <= 2048, widening _LONG_SEGMENT_ENTRIES to 16,384 and _LONG_MERGE_KEYS to 16,384 while keeping total shared memory <= 47 KiB (2 CTAs/SM on SM120). This collapses 16,384-entry reindex selection to a single kernel launch (zero merge, zero scratch), cuts 524K k=512 from 128 segments + 2 merge levels to 32 segments + 1 merge level, cuts 1M k=2048 g=8 from 32 segments + 3 merge levels to 8 segments + 1 merge level, and cuts 1M k=2048 g=1 from 256 segments + 4 merge levels to 64 segments + 2 merge levels.
2. Apply a bijective XOR bank-conflict swizzle (idx ^ ((idx >> 5) & 31)) on shared-memory keys, bound load/threshold/compact loops by the active entry count n_active, and gate the second compaction read loop on (n_gt > 0) | (sel_eq > 0).
3. Add gather_scores=True on IndexerTopK so source-layer IndexerV41Plan(candidate_blocks=True) selects the top-512 positions directly from the 2,048 ascending candidate blocks published by select_blocks in a single 1-CTA-per-row launch with zero select scratch buffers.
4. Spread ordered compaction of a partly filled segment or merge group over every thread: with an active count n, each thread owns ceil(n / 512) consecutive keys instead of the compile-time 32 (so a 2,048-entry row no longer leaves 448 of 512 threads idle while 64 threads read 32 keys each, twice), and one block scan of packed (ties << 16 | above) counts replaces the two scans, the ties kept before a thread being min(ties needed, ties before it). Without this, the 16,384-entry one-pass selector (IndexerTopK(16384, 512, 1): the dense layers' short-prefill plan, rows <= 1024) was slower than 1107 at 520..4,096-entry extents with 256..1,024 rows: in 29 of 30 sampled 1,024-row prefill chunks below position 8,192, by up to 22% (19% at 4,096 entries x 1,024 rows), where its 2 CTAs/SM (32 KiB of keys) against 1107's 3 (512 threads, about 23 KiB each) left the longer per-thread compaction exposed.

Quality:
Bit-identical (torch.equal on selected indices, values, and counts) across all widths, batch sizes, partial active extents, and adversarial tie-breaking cases; preserves _SEGMENT_ENTRIES = 4096 and _MERGE_KEYS = 8192 for coarse selectors with topk > 2048. Compaction ownership changes only which thread reads which keys: positions are still written in ascending entry order, and min(ties needed, ties before) is exactly the running sum of the per-thread tie quotas the second scan computed; the packed scan is used only where both counts stay below 2**15 (per * threads < 32768).

Tests:
- pytest --noconftest -q tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_lsa.py tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_attention.py (132 passed across 2 fresh container boots).
- python3 tests/kernels/attention/deepseek_v41_indexer_reads.py (scored 4 cases across 2 fresh container boots).
- test_topk_partial_extent_compaction: tie-heavy rows at 513..16,383-entry extents (one pass, dense and candidate rows) and 2..32 live merge lists (524,288 wide) against the reference selection.
- On the candidate-49 stack (sp8, 2 boots): the pytest command above, 142 passed, 1 skipped, 1 xfailed (the stack's other patches add tests); bench_2boot.py's exactness check PASS; every timed cell of the short-extent sweep and the served-shape gap bench torch.equal to 1107.

Upstream status: local SM120 TileLang long-context indexer top-k optimization.
